🚨🔴 Manual Call Point (MCP) Spacing Calculation 📊

A Manual Call Point (MCP) allows occupants to manually activate the fire alarm system during an emergency. Proper spacing ensures quick and easy access.

📘 General Design Principle

Manual Call Points should be installed:

✅ Along escape routes and near exits
✅ At every floor exit and stairwell entrance
✅ At a mounting height of approximately 1.2–1.5 m above finished floor level (subject to local code)

📏 Typical Spacing

A common design practice is that the travel distance to the nearest MCP should not exceed 30 m (always verify with the applicable fire code and local authority requirements).

🧮 Example

🔹 Maximum Travel Distance = 30 m
🔹 Corridor Length = 90 m

✅ Minimum MCPs Required = 90 ÷ 30 = 3 MCPs

(Final locations should also consider exits, staircases, and building layout.)

📋 Factors Affecting MCP Quantity

🏢 Building Layout
🚪 Exit Door Locations
📏 Travel Distance Requirements
🧱 Obstructions & Partitions
📘 Fire Code Requirements

📌 Applications

🏢 Office Buildings
🏨 Hotels
🏥 Hospitals
🏫 Schools
🏭 Industrial Facilities

📋 Design Checklist

✅ Maximum Travel Distance
✅ Exit & Staircase Locations
✅ Mounting Height
✅ Visibility & Accessibility
✅ Compliance with Fire Codes

💡 Tip: Always install MCPs near every exit and ensure the required maximum travel distance is not exceeded. Final spacing and installation should comply with NFPA 72, BS 5839, or the applicable local fire code.
